#X text 9 8 This subpatch saves the values of each GUI control on save of the module's parent patch., f 88;
#N canvas 0 22 450 300 savestateDetails 0;
#X text 9 8 The [savestate] object works by sending a "bang" out its right outlet when the patch it resides in is saved. We use that "bang" to develop a list of parameters to save \, this list is then sent to the left inlet of [savestate] and is stored after the patch is closed. When the patch is opened \, that list is output on load \, and we distribute the parameters to the objects in the patch., f 130;
#X text 9 78 All parameters whose values are configured to be received in the [savestateStoreParams] subpatch will have their values compiled into a list at patch save - facilated by [savestate]'s "bang" message \, and stored. When the patch is opened \, that list will be distributed to all the correct objects as long as the [send] objects in [savestateOutputParameters] are configured to correctly send the parameters to the objects in the same order as they were stored in the list at save., f 131;
#X text 4 262 For tdh.lib modules \, it is convention that all GUIs with both a slider and numberbox only store the numberbox value \, as it will automatically update the slider value., f 132;
#X text 9 158 This subpatch facilitates an additional feature for saving parameters \, in that it relies on an external [toggle] that will activate or deactivate parameter loading. All parameters are saved regardless of the toggle's state \, but parameters are only loaded at patch open when the [toggle] is checked., f 131;
#X text 9 218 The [toggle]'s state is saved with the patch as the last element in the parameter list \, and at patch open \, this list item is trimmed off the list and used to open or close a [spigot] \, determining if the parameters are reported to their objects or not., f 131;
#X restore 409 39 pd savestateDetails;
