#X text 29 384 To compare the input value to values indicated to match \, we need a select object for each value to match. To get the matching values from the list input to the select objects \, we use [list split 2] and split off the first element of the list \, then pass the list on to another [list split 2] where we take the next element of the list (now the first element of the list) and send that off to select \, then repeat the process.;
#X text 29 514 The number of values set to be compared for matches is variable \, so we use dynamic patching to generate the correct number of [list split 2] \, [select] \, and [outlet] objects.;
